Celestial Light						CATEGORY:FEAT		TYPE:Bloodline					PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Celestial Bloodline		PRESPELLTYPE:1,Arcane=2		DESC:Cast Light as a spell-like ability.			SPELLS:INNATE|TIMES=5|TIMEUNIT=Day|Light,11+CHA
Charming							CATEGORY:FEAT		TYPE:General					PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Negotiator				PRESTAT:1,CHA=13		DESC:When you make a charisma check to exert control over the target of a mind-affecting spell you cast, gain +3 to this roll.  This applies to checks to convince the target of a Charm spell to do something they would not normally do, as well as opposed charisma checks make by two spellcasters affecting the same target. 
Circle Student						CATEGORY:FEAT		TYPE:General.Fighter					PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Dodge	PRESKILL:1,Concentration=2	PRETOTALAB:4	DESC:When you designate a target for Dodge, you may increase the dodge bonus to AC by 1, and gain a +1 competence bonus to hit that creature, but you take -2 to AC vs all other creatures. 
Circle Master						CATEGORY:FEAT		TYPE:General.Fighter					PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Dodge		PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Circle Student		PRESKILL:1,Concentration=4	PRETOTALAB:8		DESC:Increase the AC and attack bonuses granted by circle student by 1.
Combat CHarm						CATEGORY:FEAT		TYPE:General							PRESTAT:1,WIS=13		DESC:When you cast a Charm spell in combat on a creature threatened by you or your allies, the target does not gain the usual +5 bonus to its save against the spell.
Commanding							CATEGORY:FEAT		TYPE:General							PRESTAT:1,CHA=15		PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Persuasive		DESC:+1 t save DCs for Enchantment(Compulsion) spells.		BONUS:DC|SUBSCHOOL.Compulsion|1\
Cuthbert's Smite					CATEGORY:FEAT		TYPE:General					PREDEITY:1,St. Cuthbert		PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,TYPE.PaladinSmiteEvil		BONUS:VAR|SmiteEvilTimes|1	DESC:You may smite chaos as well as evil, and may smite an additional time per day.
Cutpurse							CATEGORY:FEAT		TYPE:General			PRESKILL:1,Sleight Of Hand=5		PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Improved Unarmed Strike		DESC:You may disguise sleight-of-hand attempts as combat maneuves.  You may use sleight-of-hand to pickpocket enemy combatants without provoking an attack of opportunity.
Dead Eye							CATEGORY:FEAT		TYPE:General			PRESTAT:1,DEX=17	PRETOTALAB:14		PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Weapon Focus		PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Point Blank Shot			DESC:You can add your dexterity bonus to ranged attacks with weapons you have weapon focus with, as long as the target is not immune to critical hits and is within 30'
Deceptive Dodge						CATEGORY:FEAT		TYPE:General			PRETOTALAB:4	PRESTAT:1,DEX=13		PRESTAT:1,INT=13			PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Dodge		DESC:When a melee attack by the subject of your dodge feat misses you while you are fighting defensively, that attack has a chance to strike another target of your choice that is adjacent to both you and the attacker.  The attacker must make a new attack roll for the redirected attack, using the same modifiers applied to the missed attack.  You may use this feat oncer per round.
Divine Fervor						CATEGORY:FEAT		TYPE:General		PREDEITY:1,Y		DESC:1/Day, gain +2 to one ability score.  Lasts 1+Charisma Modifier rounds, minimum 1. 
Divine Conduit						CATEGORY:FEAT		TYPE:General	PRESTAT:1,CHA=13		PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Divine Fervor		PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Special Ability,Turn Undead,Rebuke Undead		DESC:Touch a divine spellcaster who worships the same deity and expend a number of Turn attempts.  These can be used as spell levels by the target to apply a metamagic feat to the next spell they cast.  Spell takes its normal time to cast, obviating Quicken Spell. 
AC Bonus				KEY:Battle Dancer ~ AC Bonus					CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.BattleDancer Class Feature.SpecialQuality.BattleDancerAC											DEFINE:BattleDancerACLVL|0	DEFINE:BattleDancerACBonus|0	DEFINE:BattleDancerStatBonus|0										DESC:A BattleDancer is highly trained at dodging blows, and she has a sixth sense that lets her avoid even unanticipated attacks. When unarmored and unencumbered, the BattleDancer adds her Charisma bonus (if any) to her AC. In addition, a BattleDancer gains a +1 bonus to AC at 5th level. This bonus increases by 1 for every five BattleDancer levels thereafter (+2 at 10th, +3 at 15th, and +4 at 20th level). These bonuses to AC apply even against touch attacks or when the BattleDancer is flat-footed. She loses these bonuses when she is immobilized or helpless, when she wears any armor, when she carries a shield, or when she carries a medium or heavy load.																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																BONUS:COMBAT|AC|BattleDancerACBonus|PREVAREQ:ENCUMBERANCE,0,var("COUNT[EQTYPE.ARMOR.EQUIPPED]"),0																					BONUS:VAR|BattleDancerACBonus|BattleDancerStatBonus+(BattleDancerACLVL/5)	BONUS:VAR|BattleDancerStatBonus|max(CHA,0)	BONUS:VAR|BattleDancerACLVL|BattleDancerLVL								SOURCEPAGE:p.40
Bonus Speed			KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Fast Movement				CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Extraordinary.Class Feature.BattleDancer Class Feature.SpecialQuality											DEFINE:BattleDancerMoveLVL|0	DEFINE:BattleDancerMoveBonus|0														DESC:At 3rd level, a Battle Dancer gains an enhancement bonus to her speed, as shown on Table 3-10. A Battle Dancer in armor (even light armor) or carrying a medium or heavy load loses this extra speed.																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																																								BONUS:MOVEADD|TYPE.Walk|BattleDancerMoveBonus|TYPE=Enhancement|PREVAREQ:ENCUMBERANCE,0,var("COUNT[EQTYPE.ARMOR.EQUIPPED]"),0	BONUS:VAR|BattleDancerMoveLVL|BattleDancerLVL	BONUS:VAR|BattleDancerMoveBonus|((BattleDancerMoveLVL+2)/6)*10													SOURCEPAGE:p.41
Unarmed Strike			KEY:Battle Dancer ~ Unarmed Strike				CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:Class Feature.Battle Dancer Class Feature.SpecialQuality																																			DESC:Battle Dancers are highly trained in fighting unarmed, giving them considerable advantages when doing so. At 1st level, a Battle Dancer gains Improved Unarmed Strike as a bonus feat. A Battle Dancer's attacks may be with either fist interchangeably or even from elbows, knees, and feet. This means that a Battle Dancer may even make unarmed strikes with her hands full. There is no such thing as an off-hand attack for a Battle Dancer striking unarmed. A Battle Dancer may thus apply her full Strength bonus on damage rolls for all her unarmed strikes. Usually a Battle Dancer's unarmed strikes deal lethal damage, but she can choose to deal nonlethal damage instead with no penalty on her attack roll. She has the same choice to deal lethal or nonlethal damage while grappling. A Battle Dancer's unarmed strike is treated both as a manufactured weapon and a natural weapon for the purpose of spells and effects that enhance or improve either manufactured weapons or natural weapons (such as the magic fang and magic weapon spells). A Battle Dancer also deals more damage with her unarmed strikes than a normal person would, as shown on Table 3-10: The Battle Dancer. The unarmed damage on Table 3-10 is for Medium Battle Dancers. A Small Battle Dancer deals less damage than the amount given there with her unarmed attacks, while a Large Battle Dancer deals more damage; see Table: Small or Large Battle Dancer Unarmed Damage.																																																																																																																																																																																																																					ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Improved Unarmed Strike|!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=ACF,TYPE.Battle DancerImprovedUnarmedStrike																																																																																																								SOURCEPAGE:p.41
Battle Dancer ~ Unarmed Damage	CATEGORY:Internal		DEFINE:BattleDancerUnarmedDamageProgression|0	DEFINE:BattleDancerUnarmedDamageLVL|0	DEFINE:BattleDancerUnarmedDamageLevel|0	BONUS:VAR|BattleDancerUnarmedDamageLevel|BattleDancerLVL	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|Battle Dancer Unarmed Damage LVL 1|PREVAREQ:BattleDancerUnarmedDamageProgression,0	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|Battle Dancer Unarmed Damage LVL 4|PREVAREQ:BattleDancerUnarmedDamageProgression,1	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|Battle Dancer Unarmed Damage LVL 8|PREVAREQ:BattleDancerUnarmedDamageProgression,2	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|Battle Dancer Unarmed Damage LVL 12|PREVAREQ:BattleDancerUnarmedDamageProgression,3	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|Battle Dancer Unarmed Damage LVL 16|PREVAREQ:BattleDancerUnarmedDamageProgression,4	ABILITY:Internal|AUTOMATIC|Battle Dancer Unarmed Damage LVL 20|PREVAREQ:BattleDancerUnarmedDamageProgression,5	BONUS:VAR|BattleDancerUnarmedDamageLVL|BattleDancerLVL	BONUS:VAR|BattleDancerUnarmedDamageProgression|(min(5,BattleDancerUnarmedDamageLVL/4))
